# Customer data exports (audit ZIP drops, etc.) — never commit these
docs/*.zip

# Local marketing/showoff assets
assets/
screenshots/
docs/screenshots/

# Local agent-runner metadata. Product skills under `.agents/skills/` are source
# artifacts and must remain addable when EchoSEO ships a new workflow.
/.agents/AGENTS.md

# --- AgentKit project plugin (personal, not committed) ---
.agentkit/
.claude-plugin/
ak-engineer/

# Local agent-runner drops land inside .agents/skills/ alongside the product's
# own skills, and the two are indistinguishable by path. Ignoring everything is
# what keeps a stray `git add -A` from committing dozens of a developer's local
# tools into a public repository; the shipped skills are unaffected because git
# keeps honouring files it already tracks.
#
# Adding a NEW product skill therefore needs `git add -f .agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
.agents/skills/*/*
